    "label": "th:problem-dependent",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "For the $N$-armed stochastic bandit problem, Thompson Sampling algorithm has expected regret $$\\Ex[{\\cal R}(T)] \\leq (1+\\epsilon) \\sum_{i=2}^N \\frac{\\ln T}{d(\\mu_i,\\mu_1)} \\Delta_i+ O(\\frac{N}{\\epsilon^2})  $$ in time $T$, where $d(\\mu_i,\\mu_1)=\\mu_i \\log \\frac{\\mu_i}{\\mu_1} + (1-\\mu_i) \\log \\frac{(1-\\mu_i)}{(1-\\mu_1)}$. The big-Oh notation in above assumes $\\mu_i, \\Delta_i, i=1, \\ldots, N$ to be constants."
   },
